SULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 MAY 97 at 15 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a modified radical mastectomy specimen with a 28 x 10 8cm ellipse of white skin containing a 2 7cm in diameter distorted nipple and areola  The surrounding 7 x 6cm skin is firm  darkened and contains a REMOVED_DATE x 1cm ulceration inferomedially and a 3 3cm linear indentation   scar   lateral to the nipple  The fibroadipose tissue deep to the skin measures 24 x 17 x 8 5cm and is contiguous with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm axillary tail  Deep to the firm area on the skin is an 8 x 7 x 5cm tan to white  firm  ill defined mass  Strands of tan tissue approach to within 0 5cm of the superior and inferior super