ing of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 07     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     NOTE  Because of an apparent discrepancy between the size of the tumor measured radiographically  2 5 to 3 0cm   and the size of the invasive tumor recorded on the pathology report  the specimen is retrieved and an additional three sections are examined  X Z   A 3cm gross abnormality is identified  but it is composed histologically of a 1 5cm invasive component surrounded by proliferative fibrocystic changes and comedocarcinoma in situ  with a fibrotic periductal response   Added by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 53 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  excision right breast tumor   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm portion of breast with a 1 5cm stellate  firm and gritty mass  located in the middle portion of the specimen  and 0 5cm from the anterior posterior margins  and away from all other margins  A representative section is frozen as FX  1 and saved frozen  Section code  A B  tumor and anterior margin C D  tumor and posterior margin E  superior margin F  medial margin Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and  right axillary nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of adipose tissue from which 13 tan pink lymph nodes are identified ranging from 0 5cm in greatest dimension up to